exit=0
--- stdout ---
Show the newest lines of the gateway's own log file (GET /logs),
printed oldest to newest so they read like the tail of the file.

The gateway reads the file backwards from its end. --level and --keyword
are case-sensitive substring filters combined with AND; with a filter set
the gateway keeps scanning back until --lines matching lines are found,
the start of the file is reached, or its per-request scan budget is spent.
When older lines remain, the last line of output names the --file and
--cursor to pass for the next (older) page; keep the filters unchanged
from page to page. --file reads one of the files listed by
'loxicmd get log-archives' instead of the current log. With -o json the
gateway's body is printed verbatim.

ex)
	loxicmd get logs
	loxicmd get logs --lines 500 --level ERROR
	loxicmd get logs --keyword timeout --file gateway.log.1.gz
	loxicmd get logs -o json

Usage:
  loxicmd get logs [flags]

Flags:
      --cursor string    Cursor printed by the previous page, for the next older page
      --file string      Log file to read, by name as listed by 'get log-archives' (default: the current log)
  -h, --help             help for logs
      --keyword string   Keep only lines containing this text (case-sensitive)
      --level string     Keep only lines containing this level text (case-sensitive)
      --lines int        Matching lines to return (up to 10000) (default 100)

Global Flags:
  -s, --apiserver string    Set API server IP address (default "127.0.0.1")
      --bearer              Send the token as 'Authorization: Bearer <token>' (required by the inference gateway; disable for classic loxilb raw-token targets) (default true)
      --cacert string       CA certificate (PEM) to verify the server (https only)
      --cert string         Client certificate (PEM) for mutual TLS (https only)
  -k, --insecure            Skip TLS certificate verification (https only)
      --key string          Client private key (PEM) for mutual TLS (https only)
  -o, --output string       Set output layer (ex.) wide, json)
  -p, --port int            Set API server port number (default 11111)
      --protocol string     Set API server http/https (default "http")
  -t, --timeout int16       Set timeout (default 10)
      --token string        Set Token for the API server (deprecated: the value is visible in shell history and process listings; use --token-file)
      --token-file string   Read the API server token from an owner-only (0600) regular file; replaces the deprecated --token
